*.sh text eol=lf
templates/pre-push text eol=lf
# VERSION was the one tracked extensionless file with no eol rule, so a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true landed it as CRLF. Every tool that reads it
# strips \r defensively, but the test that asserts <removed-packer> uses it did not
# — which is why that test failed on every Windows run in this repo's history
# and was written off as unrelated. Pinned here so the file is LF everywhere.
VERSION text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf

# ledger.jsonl is append-only JSONL and is deliberately NOT union-merged. Union kept every line but
# lost the order the verdicts depend on (ours-then-theirs, so "latest" followed merge direction):
# a newer FAIL read PASS, a restart from one branch lowered another's tier floor, a sibling branch's
# pass cleared this branch's FAIL (the kit's risk register, R-008). Without it two branches that both log
# gates conflict, which makes a person look. Keep both sides' lines in the order they were logged,
# then re-run `compliance` and re-log any gate whose pass came from the other branch.
